  "invariants": [
    "PromptOS catalogs and resolves skills; it does not grant execution authority.",
    "Every app remains the authority owner for its own product-specific skills.",
    "Shared skills are references to ULTRATHINK source packages, not copied app instructions.",
    "Skill discovery is not installation, execution, approval, or authorization.",
    "A skill must explicitly declare compatibility with the requesting app.",
    "External skills remain quarantined until their independent intake gates pass.",
    "Shared operating skills resolve only for authorized repository operators and are never implicitly exposed to product end users.",
    "Proposed app-owned skill IDs are planning placeholders until their exact source packages pass repository audit; resolution does not mean installed or active.",
    "FCR remains the portfolio governance and approval authority; PromptOS must not create a competing approval or distribution authority.",
    "A partial repository skill audit is not evidence of absence; every app profile carries explicit audit coverage and source repositories."
  ],
